      {
        "narration": "Maya plants a bean seed in a cup at school. She wants to know what it needs to grow. Let's find out together.",
        "text": "What plants need",
        "visual": { "kind": "emoji", "emoji": "🌱", "count": null, "filled": null }
      },
      {
        "narration": "Maya gives the seed some water. Plants need water to grow. Roots take it in from the soil. Without water, a plant droops and dries out.",
        "text": "Water",
        "visual": { "kind": "emoji", "emoji": "💧", "count": null, "filled": null }
      },
      {
        "narration": "Maya puts the cup on a sunny windowsill. Plants need light and air. Leaves use light and air to make food. The sun also gives heat, and plants need to stay warm.",
        "text": "Light, air, and heat",
        "visual": { "kind": "emoji", "emoji": "☀️", "count": null, "filled": null }
      },
      {
        "narration": "Soil holds nutrients. Nutrients are minerals in soil that help a plant grow strong. Roots take them in with water. The plant makes its own food with light and air. Plain sand has fewer nutrients.",
        "text": "Nutrients",
        "visual": { "kind": "emoji", "emoji": "🌱", "count": null, "filled": null }
      },
      {
        "narration": "Soon Maya's beans grow bigger. Plants also need space. Roots and leaves need room to spread out. When plants are packed too close, they have to share, and they grow poorly.",
        "text": "Space",
        "visual": { "kind": "objects", "emoji": "🌱", "count": 5, "filled": null }
      },
      {
        "narration": "A plant can be hurt by no water, too much cold, too little light, or a crowded pot. Maya checks her plant every day. Now it's your turn to practise.",
        "text": "Let's practise!",
        "visual": null
      }
